        "Instead of keeping every method in your head, store the instructions in a form you can inspect and improve.",
        "A prompt library reduces the effort of starting from scratch and makes your workflow more consistent.\n9.2 Organise prompts by job\nA simple structure:\nAI Prompt Library/\n    01 - Thinking and Learning/\n        Intellectual Sparring Partner\n        First-Principles Thought Partner\n        Research Coach",
        "02 - Business/\n        Customer Research Coach\n        Offer Creation Coach\n        Product Development Coach\n        Business Advisor",
        "03 - Content/\n        Personal Brand Coach\n        Content Idea Generator\n        Newsletter Coach\n        Copywriting Assistant",
        "04 - YouTube/\n        Title Research\n        Video Outline\n        Introduction\n        Script\n        B-roll\n        Description",
        "05 - Operations/\n        Project Planning\n        Process Documentation\n        Decision Review\nThis is an example organisation, not a required software structure. Use whatever storage method makes prompts easy to find, update, and reuse.\n9.3 Store the full context with important prompts\nA prompt may depend on more than its main instruction.",
        "Store supporting information where relevant:\n- The expert guide.\n- Example material.\n- Your preferences.\n- Your brand or business context.\n- Quality criteria.\n- Output format.\n- Known limitations.\n- A version history.\nKeep sensitive information out of prompts unless it is necessary and the AI tool is appropriate for handling it.\n9.4 Version and improve prompts\nWhen a prompt produces a weak result, do not simply add random instructions.",
        "Diagnose the failure:\n- Was the task unclear?\n- Was context missing?\n- Was the method incomplete?\n- Did the model misunderstand the reference?\n- Were the examples too narrow?\n- Was the output format ambiguous?\n- Was the quality standard not measurable?\nThen update the relevant section.",
        "A simple version record:\n| Version | Change | Reason | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1.0 | Initial prompt | First working version | Baseline |\n| 1.1 | Added context questions | Output lacked customer details | More relevant output |\n| 1.2 | Added quality checklist | Drafts contained unsupported claims | Easier review |",
