        "The difference between basic and advanced AI use is not simply knowing more prompt tricks. It is understanding how to define a task, teach a method, supply context, and build a repeatable process.",
        "The full system is:\n1. Choose the task: Identify something you want AI to help you do.\n2. Define quality: Decide what a good result actually looks like.\n3. Develop instructions: Write your own method, ask AI for a guide, extract an expert method, or analyse an example.\n4. Create the prompt: Use a meta-prompt to turn those instructions into a reusable system.\n5. Gather context: Make the prompt interview you before it acts.\n6. Execute: Apply the method to your real situation.\n7. Review: Check the output and correct mistakes.\n8. Save: Add the improved prompt to your library.\n9. Repeat: Use the process to build coaches, advisors, thought partners, and business workflows.\nThe most important shift is from asking AI to guess what you want to teaching it how to help you achieve it.",
